Package: swbrd-dtls-proxy
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Evan Brass <brassevan@gmail.com>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: swbrd-common (>= @COMPAT@), systemd, init-system-helpers (>= 1.54), libssl3t64 (>= 3.5), libc6 (>= 2.38), libgcc-s1
Recommends: swbrd-cert-rotate
Homepage: https://github.com/evan-brass/swbrd
Description: DTLS proxy that uses destination IP+port as the connection id
 Terminates DTLS for clients that aim at a random address inside a routed /96,
 standing in for DTLS connection ids, and forwards the plaintext to the host's
 SCTP-over-UDP endpoint.  Uses the shared IP_TRANSPARENT divert rules from
 swbrd-common; it installs no nftables tables of its own.
 .
 Built for one private host and not fit for redistribution; see
 /usr/share/doc/swbrd-dtls-proxy/copyright.
